WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.976
Now it is time to plant. Timing, depth and spacing all matter.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.920
Plant at the start of the rainy season, so cuttings have moisture to grow roots.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.643
Space plants about one metre apart in each direction.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.572
Push each cutting into the soil with the buds pointing up.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.640
Bury about two-thirds of the cutting, upright or at a slant.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.653
After two to three weeks, replace any cuttings that did not sprout.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:34.327
Before you move on, check: Plant at the start of the rains. Space about 1 m apart. Fill gaps after 2 to 3 weeks.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.928
In the next lesson: Caring for young cassava.
